CORE
main.py
--function first_or --unwind 5 --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
dereference failure.*: FAILURE$
--
The --function harness passed a dangling nondet pointer for a list
argument and for the list and object slots of an untyped argument; every
access failed the pointer checks. A caller can only pass valid objects, so
these now point to fresh objects with nondet contents.
